# Drive the SR10.4 cartridge's install environment one step further than
# `tools/cartridge-boot.script`: past `RBAK_BS`'s own prompt, so the restore
# actually starts.
#
# Kept separate from `cartridge-boot.script` on purpose. That file is a
# *reference* — it reproduces the transcript `PROJECT_STATUS.md` prints, and
# answering a prompt it never answered would make it reproduce something else.
# This one is the install route's first step.
#
# The `Y` is the answer to
#
#     *** This program will replace system software on your disk.
#     Do you wish to proceed? (Y/N):
#
# which is why the disk this runs against **must be a copy**. RBAK writes to it.
#
# `tools/md-shell.script`'s banner rule applies unchanged: MD prints `\r\n>`
# after its sign-on and discards what is typed while it is still printing, so
# wait for the prompt and not for the banner.
expect MD7C
expect >
send DI C\r
expect >
send EX DOMAIN_OS\r
expect Do you wish to proceed
send Y\r
